Here is the PlantUML class diagram:
@startuml
class Course {
  - name : String
  - credits : Integer
  + professors : Professor[]
}

class Professor {
  - name : String
  + courses : Course[]
}

class Student {
  - name : String
  + courses : Course[]
}

class Dormitory {
  - price : Float
  + students : Student[]
}

Course o--* Professor : teaches
Professor o--* Course : participates
Course *--* Student : enrolls
Student o--* Course : enrolled
Dormitory *--* Student : accommodated

@enduml
This PlantUML code represents the entities and relationships described in the requirements. The `o--*` symbol indicates an aggregation relationship (a course aggregates professors, students, etc.), while the `*--*` symbol indicates a composition relationship (a dormitory can have from one to four students).